    "definitions": {
      "short": "silliness",
      "usage": "folly, foolishly(-ness).",
      "full": "H200. ivveleth אִוֶּ֫לֶת 25 noun feminine folly. — absolute Prov 12:23 +; construct 14:8 +; suffix אִוַּלְתִּי Psa 38:6 , etc.; &#8212; folly , special product of כְּסִילִים (see כֶּסֶל ) Prov 12:23 + (12 t.); with מְּתָאִים 14:18 ; with אֱוִלִיים only 16:22 ; 27:22 for alliteration. It is bound up in mind of boy, to be removed only by rod of discipline 22:15 ; ׳א personified tears down house built by נָשִׁים חַכְמוֺת 14:1 ; it is contrasted with תְּבוּנָה 14:29 ; 15:21 . II. איל אול, ( be in front of, precede, lead ; see Thes Nö MBA 1880, 774; SBA 1882, 1175 , who compare Arabic for , אוולא ᵑ7 ; compare Sabean אול DHM Epigr. Denkm. 33. 34 ; see on the other hand Lag Or ii. p. 3; M i. p.100 & below I. אלה below) **Arabic , etc., from , see Lane.",
      "rootNote": "from the same as 191 ;",
